notes.body:
Hello @rknall, 

I'm not sure how using QTemporaryFile (without some significant refactoring and likely internal function signature changes) fixes the temp-dir issue. 

I was simply following the example for the use of g_get_tmp_dir() from MR !6039 that you approved.  That same MR introduced the regression to the Merge functionality I reported in issue #18011 that this MR attempts to resolve.

Here's the current direct use of g_get_tmp_dir():

```
$ git grep -n g_get_tmp_dir 
capture_opts.c:273:    ws_log(log_domain, log_level, "Temporary Directory  : %s", capture_opts->temp_dir && capture_opts->temp_dir[0] ? capture_opts->temp_dir : g_get_tmp_dir());
dumpcap.c:439:    fprintf(output, "                           (default: %s)\n", g_get_tmp_dir());
tshark.c:490:    fprintf(output, "                           (default: %s)\n", g_get_tmp_dir());
tshark.c:625:    constpath = g_get_tmp_dir();
ui/commandline.c:170:    fprintf(output, "                           (default: %s)\n", g_get_tmp_dir());
ui/qt/about_dialog.cpp:202:    appendRow(QStringList() << tr("Temp") << (global_capture_opts.temp_dir && global_capture_opts.temp_dir[0] ? global_capture_opts.temp_dir : g_get_tmp_dir()) << tr("untitled capture files"));
ui/qt/capture_options_dialog.cpp:216:    ui->tempDirLineEdit->setPlaceholderText(g_get_tmp_dir());
```

FWIW: One nerdy workaround for the current Merge defect is to fetch the default Temp folder with tshark and pass that value as the parameter to Wireshark's `--temp-dir`, for example:;  

```
$ ./run/tshark -G folders | grep Temp | cut -f2 
/var/folders/tv/rwqbrcr564vdd_m_klvmvcv40000gn/T/
$
$ ./run/wireshark --temp-dir $(./run/tshark -G folders | grep Temp | cut -f2 ) -r ~/Traces/part1.pcap 
...
```

A quick survey of `global_capture_opts.temp_dir` reveals a few other areas where the lack of using --temp-dir option might lead to a regression like the Merge issue: 

```
$ git grep -n global_capture_opts.temp_dir 
tshark.c:628:    if (global_capture_opts.temp_dir)
tshark.c:629:        constpath = global_capture_opts.temp_dir;
ui/qt/about_dialog.cpp:202:    appendRow(QStringList() << tr("Temp") << (global_capture_opts.temp_dir && global_capture_opts.temp_dir[0] ? global_capture_opts.temp_dir : g_get_tmp_dir()) << tr("untitled capture files"));
ui/qt/capture_options_dialog.cpp:217:    ui->tempDirLineEdit->setText(global_capture_opts.temp_dir);
ui/qt/capture_options_dialog.cpp:966:        global_capture_opts.temp_dir = qstring_strdup(tempdir);
ui/qt/capture_options_dialog.cpp:969:        global_capture_opts.temp_dir = NULL;
ui/qt/export_pdu_dialog.cpp:41:    do_export_pdu(filter.constData(), global_capture_opts.temp_dir, tap_name.constData());
ui/qt/import_text_dialog.cpp:514:    import_info_.wdh = wtap_dump_open_tempfile(global_capture_opts.temp_dir, &tmp, "import", file_type_subtype, WTAP_UNCOMPRESSED, &params, &err, &err_info);
ui/qt/main_window.cpp:1080:    if (cf_merge_files_to_tempfile(this, global_capture_opts.temp_dir, &tmpname, static_cast<int>(local_files.size()),
ui/qt/main_window.cpp:1277:            merge_status = cf_merge_files_to_tempfile(this, global_capture_opts.temp_dir, &tmpname, 2, in_filenames, file_type, FALSE);
ui/qt/main_window.cpp:1282:            merge_status = cf_merge_files_to_tempfile(this, global_capture_opts.temp_dir, &tmpname, 2, in_filenames, file_type, TRUE);
ui/qt/main_window.cpp:1287:            merge_status = cf_merge_files_to_tempfile(this, global_capture_opts.temp_dir, &tmpname, 2, in_filenames, file_type, TRUE);
ui/qt/strip_headers_dialog.cpp:42:    do_export_pdu(filter.constData(), global_capture_opts.temp_dir, tap_name.constData());
```
I could see a case for introducing our own method to return a temp-dir in place of testing global_capture_opts.temp_dir directly.

Thoughts?

